 "MODESTY (do this exactly): the SAME filament-net veil continues UNBROKEN across the hips and upper thighs — the identical glowing net WEAVE, the same folds, the same fabric as the rest of the veil — but in that region the net DENSIFIES so it reads OPAQUE (you cannot see the body through it there), then GRADUALLY FADES back to sheer translucence ABOVE the waistline and BELOW mid-thigh: a SMOOTH OPACITY GRADIENT within ONE continuous piece of gossamer, with NO hard edge. The luminous net pattern stays VISIBLE even in the opaque zone — it is the VEILWEAVE ITSELF getting denser there, not a different material. LIGHTING: the opaque zone is lit the SAME as the rest of the veil — since here the wearer is WELL-LIT and the veil glows bright, the dense zone is a soft LUMINOUS WHITE fade (a bright, pale, matte white densification of the same net), NOT a dark patch, NOT a shadow, NOT grey. (General rule for future renders: the dense zone matches the veil's brightness — a WHITE fade when the veil is bright, dark only when the wearer is in darkness.) It stays soft and matte, not glittery. It is NOT a separate wrap, sarong, skirt, sash, loincloth or solid plain-cloth garment; NOT a fitted brief/thong/underwear/waistband; NOT a small patch at the crotch — just the one veil, its net thickening to a pale luminous opaque over the hips and thighs and feathering back out to sheer.\n"
 "He refracts into about FIVE-to-SIX overlapping misregistered WHOLE copies drifting around him (his signature effect), each identical — and EVERY copy holds its OWN identical THE ANSWER polearm in hand (all the figures are armed with the same weapon, NOT just the central one; no copy is empty-handed).\n"
